========================================
     KAGU RESTAURANT - DAILY MENU
========================================
STARTERS:
  Bug Soup ..................... 2 CPU cycles
  Memory Leak Salad ........... 3 CPU cycles
  Stack Overflow Nachos ....... 4 CPU cycles
MAIN COURSES:
  Kernel Panic Pasta .......... 7 CPU cycles
  Grilled Process with Scheduler Sauce .. 8 cycles
  Mutex Locked Lobster ........ 12 CPU cycles
DESSERTS:
  Deadlock Donuts ............. 3 CPU cycles
  Segfault Sundae ............. 4 CPU cycles
  Chef Kagu recommends: Kernel Panic Pasta!
Welcome to Kagu's Restaurant!
Where every dish is cooked with love and syscalls.

Our chef, the magnificent Kagu bird,
started from a humble food truck (bootloader)
and built this fine dining establishment (kernel).

Today's special: Fresh File System Fondue
Reservation? Just open() a table!
Bon appetit!
TOP SECRET RECIPE: Kernel Panic Pasta
======================================
Ingredients:
  - 1 cup of uninitialized memory
  - 2 tbsp of null pointer dereference
  - A pinch of race condition
  - 3 threads (unsynchronized)
Instructions:
  1. Fork() the process twice
  2. Mix all ingredients without mutex
  3. Heat to exactly 0xDEADBEEF degrees
  4. Serve immediately before watchdog timer expires
  5. If segfault occurs, restart from step 1
WARNING: Do not attempt without proper exception handling!
Chef Kagu's note: This dish crashes every time. Delicious!
======= KAGU RESTAURANT REVIEWS =======
***** "Best kernel-level dining!" - Process #1
**** "Food was great but had to wait() for my table" - PID 42
***** "The mutex locked lobster was worth the deadlock!" - Thread 7
*** "My dessert caused a segfault. 10/10 would dine again" - User 404
***** "Chef Kagu really knows how to handle interrupts" - IRQ Handler
**** "Great food but the scheduler kept preempting my meal" - PID 99
***** "The root beer is amazing with the right permissions" - sudo
* "I got a SIGKILL before finishing my appetizer" - PID 666
***** "Came for the Bug Soup, stayed for the Nachos" - Dev #1
**** "The piped output tea pairs well with grep salad" - bash
*** "Reservation system needs better file descriptors" - SysAdmin

Overall rating: 4.2 out of 5 stars
Open daily from boot to shutdown!
======= KAGU RESTAURANT STAFF =======
Head Chef:    Kagu Bird ............ PID 1
Sous Chef:    Init Process ......... PID 0
Waiter:       Shell ................ stdin/stdout
Bartender:    /dev/random
Dishwasher:   Garbage Collector
Bouncer:      Firewall
Accountant:   /proc/meminfo
Host:         localhost
Night Cook:   Daemon (never goes home)
