Chef Kagu's Personal Notes
==========================
TODO: Fix the race condition in the kitchen
NOTE: The mutex locked lobster recipe needs more testing
IDEA: What if we served processes in round-robin order?
BUG: Sometimes the soup fork()s itself
REMINDER: Never free() the dessert twice
THOUGHT: Maybe we should try async cooking
WARNING: The dishwasher (GC) is getting slow
URGENT: We are running out of file descriptors!
Kagu Restaurant Shopping List
==============================
[ ] 512 MB of fresh RAM sticks
[ ] 1 box of null terminators
[ ] 4 cores of organic CPU
[ ] 2 liters of thermal paste sauce
[ ] 1 bag of semaphores (assorted)
[ ] 6 pipes (for interprocess cooking)
[ ] 1 new swap file (the old one is full)
[ ] 3 mutexes (non-recursive)
Dear Diary,

Day 1: Started my restaurant from a food truck.
Day 7: Learned to manage multiple orders (processes).
Day 14: Hired a scheduler to manage the kitchen queue.
Day 21: A customer complained about a deadlock in their meal.
Day 30: Expanded to a real restaurant! Got our own filesystem.
Day 45: Memory leak in the soup kitchen. Had to restart.
Day 60: Added virtual memory. Now we can serve more guests!
Day 90: Got our first Michelin star for our syscalls!
Day 120: Two stars! Our interrupt handling is top-notch.
Day 180: Three stars! Full preemptive multitasking kitchen.
Day 365: Looking back, it all started with a simple boot sector.

                                    - Chef Kagu




























































































































































































































































































































































































































































